NAME
       halt - stop the system

SYNOPSIS
       halt [OPTIONS]...

DESCRIPTION
       halt stops every service, unmounts the file systems and stops the
       machine. On RHEL 9 halt, poweroff and reboot are small front ends to
       systemd: "halt" is the same as "systemctl halt", which stops the system
       but leaves the power on (the console then says the system is halted).
       Use poweroff (or systemctl poweroff) to switch the machine off, and
       reboot to start it again. Only root can run them.

OPTIONS
       -p, --poweroff
              Switch the power off, as poweroff does, instead of only halting.

       -f, --force
              Stop at once without asking systemd to stop the services in
              order. Needed only where systemd is not running yet, such as
              the rd.break emergency shell.

EXAMPLES
              # halt -p
              # systemctl poweroff

SEE ALSO
       shutdown(8), systemctl(1), reboot(8)
